        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: build node lists with fewer forks",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: build node lists with fewer forks\n\nEvery subtest builds the node list at least twice, and each\nlist ran about 40 processes and subshells, mostly to look up\neach facet's active host and to change case and sort. Each\ndo_nodes() also counts its nodes and lists the facets again.\nOn a test VM this was 34 ms for a node list and 15 ms for the\nremote environment string.\n\nDo the lookups and joins with shell builtins and keep only one\nsort per list, which takes those to 15 ms and 5 ms. The output\nis unchanged. Do not start lsmod and awk on every log() call\nwhen libcfs is loaded.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity\nTest-Parameters: testlist=replay-single,conf-sanity\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I5fb4883a8e0520cb01e1cb57d67b9d1cd521a045\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70264\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Vitaliy Kuznetsov <vkuznetsov@ddn.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
